        "explanation": "The new authz-client provider has order 100. The default and FIPS providers have order 200, so they take precedence when present. The ASN.1 encoder and decoder are lenient in places: they accept trailing bytes and truncate oversized integers. I found no path where untrusted input bypasses an authorization or validation check, because the client only converts signatures.",
